       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 600 mg once daily is three times the maximum recommended sertraline dose for adults, which is 200 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and GI or bleeding effects. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify going above the maximum.\n\nIt may be a typo. Typical adult doses are:\n- **Depression, OCD, or anxiety:** start at 25\u201350 mg once daily, then titrate by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least a week, up to 200 mg/day.\n- **PTSD or panic disorder:** start at 25 mg once daily, then increase to 50 mg after a week and titrate from there.\n\nCould you confirm the dose you intended, and the indication if you can? If you really do mean 600 mg, please check it with your resident or attending and the pharmacist first. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order, and I can add a note with the indication or titration plan if you'd like."
